From 1bec745fc96519a5d9514d0375501a0c2927b55c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:44:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 33/34] serial: core: do not start TX on a port that is shut
 down

uart_suspend_port() clears the port's initialized flag, stops TX and RX,
drains the transmitter and calls the driver's shutdown(), which on 8250
ports releases the DMA channels. Nothing stops a write from arriving in
between: uart_write() queues the data and __uart_start() calls
start_tx(), and with 8250 DMA that hands a new descriptor to a channel
that serial8250_release_dma() is terminating and releasing. The transfer
completes on the released channel and __dma_tx_complete() runs with
dma->txchan already NULL:

  intel-lpss 0000:00:1e.0: dma_pool_destroy dma3chan1 busy
  Oops: general protection fault, kernel NULL pointer dereference 0x20
  RIP: 0010:__dma_tx_complete+0x27/0x1b0
   vchan_complete+0x2b5/0x310
   tasklet_action_common+0xc2/0x1f0
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception in interrupt

Seen on a Surface Pro 12 (Intel), whose embedded controller sits behind
serdev on an LPSS UART (dw-apb-uart with idma64): the surface_aggregator
packet layer answers EC frames from a worker, and about one suspend in
ten to fifty hit the window. With the lid closed the EC woke the tablet
every 30-60 s, so the panic came within the hour, and with panic=0 the
machine sat dead until the battery was flat.

A port that is not initialized cannot transmit: let __uart_start() only
queue the data. uart_resume_port() calls start_tx() after startup() and
sends what accumulated.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.1
---
 drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c b/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c
index c0deec0e6af4..8f2735e6f1db 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/serial_core.c
@@ -144,6 +144,16 @@ static void __uart_start(struct uart_state *state)
 	if (!port || port->flags & UPF_DEAD || uart_tx_stopped(port))
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * uart_suspend_port() clears the initialized flag, drains the
+	 * transmitter and calls the driver's shutdown(), which releases DMA
+	 * channels on 8250 ports. A write landing in that window must only
+	 * queue its data: starting TX now races with that teardown, and
+	 * uart_resume_port() calls start_tx() once the port is up again.
+	 */
+	if (!tty_port_initialized(&state->port))
+		return;
+
 	port_dev = port->port_dev;
 
 	/* Increment the runtime PM usage count for the active check below */
-- 
